{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2666 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2d36c2c43f0198d14ba0661d6ce3c449c8f7e075fd522e77065ce53a854eb396" :edb/db-before-t 2665 :edb/db-after-t 2666 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535978 50 #inst "2026-10-15T14:34:09.144Z" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186179669 1038 #edb/ref 17592186551528 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186179669 1040 #edb/ref 17592186551531 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551524 1080 "0" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551524 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551524 1083 #uuid "0903ffe2-9d1a-51b2-851e-5c852bdde114" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551525 1080 "-16" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551525 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551525 1083 #uuid "11dec961-06c9-5500-94ca-ed63d5257fb2" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551526 1080 "16" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551526 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551526 1083 #uuid "5a64aa87-c9f3-5c7f-9ab4-27eb4b5f084d" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551527 1080 "-64" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551527 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551527 1083 #uuid "74259d58-1461-5af2-a1d5-127197a771ba" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551529 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551528 1071 "![](images/51/512905447203d1d3a96781d20d586f9c4cf5cc9392fab50607b6fc77e9b00121.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,4),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,4)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(- 8 x)\\,i+(- 8 y)\\,j$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551528 1072 #uuid "a7ad19ee-c937-5a75-b1b6-4803c2c7bf3b" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551528 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_{C_1}F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r+\\int_{C_2}F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r.$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path $C_1$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$r_1(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j,$$\n\nwith $t$ running from $0$ to $2$. Along this path, $x=t$ and $y=t^{2}$. Therefore,\n\n$$F(r_1(t))=(- 8 t)\\,i+(- 8 t^{2})\\,j.$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$r_1'(t)=(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j.$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$F(r_1(t))\\cdot r_1'(t)=(- 8 t)(1)+(- 8 t^{2})(2 t)=- 16 t^{3} - 8 t.$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\\int_{C_1}F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=\\int_{0}^{2}(- 16 t^{3} - 8 t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\\left[- 4 t^{4} - 4 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{2}=-80.$$\n\n$$\\int_C F\\cdot\\mathrm{d}r=(-80)+(16)=-64.$$" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551524 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551525 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551526 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551527 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186551530 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1077 "selection" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1078 #edb/ref 17592186551527 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551529 1079 #uuid "c79e0d9e-181d-57d1-9f9a-a7533fbd082e" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551530 1080 "-80" 13194139535978 17592186045443 true] [17592186551530 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535978 17592186045443 tr